          "value": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{x+y}(y+2z)\\,dz]dA & ={\u222c}_{D}[yz+{z}^{2}]_{z=x}^{z=x+y}\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}y((x+y)-x)+((x+y)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}+2xy+{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[x{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x({x}^{2}-0)+\\frac{2}{3}({x}^{3}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}(16-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
